Subject: gvn: jnz on a long constant only tests its low 32 bits
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Base: c0818978acec60ebb6167fade60fb7012cbf20ca

The IL document says that jnz compares only the 32 least significant
bits of a long argument to zero, but dedupjmp() folded a jnz on a
constant by testing all 64 bits, so the code below took @yes:

	%x =l add 1, 4294967295
	jnz %x, @yes, @no

Regression: filnix nanofil/tests/qbe-bugs/jnz-long-const.ssa.

diff --git a/gvn.c b/gvn.c
index 2417150..a785824 100644
--- a/gvn.c
+++ b/gvn.c
@@ -416,7 +416,7 @@ dedupjmp(Fn *fn, Blk *b)
 	if (b->s1 == b->s2
 	|| isconbits(fn, b->jmp.arg, &v)
 	|| zeroval(fn, b, b->jmp.arg, Kw, &z)) {
-		if (v == 0 || z)
+		if ((int32_t)v == 0 || z)
 			b->s1 = b->s2;
 		/* we later move active ins out of dead blks */
 		b->s2 = 0;
